mdv: "1.0"
title: Quarterly review
---

# Quarterly review

Block directives are containers, so what is inside them is still Markdown and
still MDV. The grid holds two chart blocks; the callout holds a paragraph; the
figure is a leaf, and takes its caption from an attribute rather than a body.

:::mdv-grid{cols=2 gap=16}

```mdv bar
title: Revenue
x: region
y: revenue
---
region,revenue
North,120
South,84
```

```mdv line
title: Trend
x: month
y: revenue
---
month,revenue
2026-01,120
2026-02,148
```

:::

:::mdv-callout{kind=note}

The grid closes before the callout opens, so neither nests inside the other.

:::

::mdv-figure{caption="Revenue by region, 2026" id=fig-revenue}

A trailing paragraph, outside every directive.
